Telegram supports rich text formatting natively through desktop shortcuts, mobile context menus, and Markdown syntax (specifically MarkdownV2 for API and bot integration).

**Text Formatting Options & Shortcuts**

| Format Style | Native / MarkdownV2 Syntax | Keyboard Shortcut (Desktop) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Bold** | `*text*` or `**text**` | `Ctrl` + `B` |
| **Italic** | `_text_` or `*text*` | `Ctrl` + `I` |
| **Underline** | `__text__` | `Ctrl` + `U` |
| **Strikethrough** | `~text~` | `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `X` |
| **Quote** | `> text` | `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `.` |
| **Monospace** | ``code`` | `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `M` |
| **Code Block** | ````language\ncode\n```` | N/A |
| **Spoiler** | ` |  |
| **Hyperlink** | `[Link Text](https://example.com)` | `Ctrl` + `K` |
| **Date / Time** | Dynamic Entity | `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `D` |

---

**Clean Markdown Code Example**

```markdown
*This is bold text*
_This is italic text_
__This is underlined text__
~This is strikethrough text~
||This is hidden spoiler text||

> This is a single-line quote block.

`Inline monospace text`

```python
# Code block with syntax highlighting
def greet():
    print("Hello, Telegram!")

```

[Open Telegram Website](https://telegram.org)

```

---

**Supported File & Media Formats**

Beyond text formatting, Telegram allows uploading almost any standard file format as a document or playable media, up to **2 GB** (or **4 GB** for Premium accounts):

* **Images & Stickers:** JPG, PNG, WEBP, TGS (animated stickers), GIF, SVG, HEIC
* **Audio & Voice:** MP3, FLAC, WAV, OGG, M4A, OPUS
* **Video & Video Messages:** MP4, MOV, MKV, AVI, WEBM
* **Documents & Archives:** PDF, DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, TXT, ZIP, RAR, 7Z, TAR

```